    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should strongly consider accepting this offer.** \n\nSecuring a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** alongside a $1.08M equity grant at Google L6 without a competing written offer is a massive win. You pushed for your unvested equity to be made whole, and Google responded with a top-of-market concession.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\n| Component | Meta (Current) | Google (Revised Offer) | Difference |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | Match |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | +$12,000/yr |\n| **New Equity (Y1)** | ~$200,000\u2013$250,000 | $270,000 (flat) *or* ~$356,000 (front-loaded)* | +$20,000 to +$106,000 |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | **+$200,000** |\n| **Total Year 1 Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$758,000 \u2013 $844,000** | **+$232,000 to +$318,000 (+44% to +60%)** |\n\n*\\*Google standard GSU vesting is often front-loaded (33% Y1 / 33% Y2 / 22% Y3 / 12% Y4).*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Why This is an Exceptional Outcome\n\n1. **You Got Full Cash Replacement for Paper Risk:** Walking away from unvested equity usually involves trading one set of volatile RSUs for another. By securing $200k in **guaranteed cash**, you fully neutralize your lost Meta RSUs in Year 1 while still receiving a fresh $1.08M stock grant.\n2. **You Hit the Negotiation Ceiling:** A $200,000 sign-on bonus is at the extreme high end of what Google compensation committees approve for L6. Pushing further on base or equity at this stage carries diminishing returns and risks friction with hiring managers.\n3. **Four-Year Value Creation:** Over 4 years, your guaranteed floor at Google (assuming target bonus and stock price parity) is approximately **$2.5M+**, significantly outperforming your current baseline at Meta before factoring in stock appreciation.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Things to Clarify Before You Sign\n\nBefore giving your verbal acceptance, ask the recruiter to clarify these details in writing:\n\n1. **Sign-On Payout Structure & Clawback:**\n   * Is the $200,000 paid as a single lump sum in your first 30\u201360 days, or is it split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k Y1 / $100k Y2)?\n   * What is the clawback period? (Standard is typically 12 months for Year 1 payouts).\n2. **Equity Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Confirm if it's monthly vesting with a front-loaded schedule (33/33/22/12) or flat (25% per year). \n3. **Team & Scope:**\n   * Make sure you are 100% aligned with the hiring manager, team mandate, and scope. Culture and organizational momentum matter just as much as compensation once you make the jump.\n\n---\n\n### Recommendation\n\n**Accept the offer.** You took a passive outreach and leveraged it into a Year 1 compensation package of roughly **$750k\u2013$840k**. \n\nLet the recruiter know you appreciate their partnership in getting the sign-on approved, confirm the payout details, and sign.",
